<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Lodi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1796</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> was fought on 10 May 1796 at the bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adda-river">Adda</a> at Lodi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s French army stormed the crossing against the rearguard of the retreating Austrian army. The victory opened the way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, which Bonaparte entered on 15 May, and greatly increased his prestige with his soldiers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-lodi.jpg" alt="Battle of Lodi" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis-François, Baron Lejeune · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Lodi,_10_May_1796_(by_Louis-Fran%C3%A7ois_Lejeune).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
